  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0025","idiomatic","The emperor agreed and appointed Xiangru commandant of palace attendants, giving him the credenza and dispatching him as chief envoy.","The emperor agreed and appointed Xiangru General of the Household, sending him as an envoy bearing imperial credentials.","建節往使 means Xiangru went as an envoy bearing imperial credentials; “credenza” is an unrelated furniture word, and the source does not make him a chief envoy.","high","applied"],
    ["s0047","idiomatic","If your words were true, Shu would never have adopted Han costume nor Ba Han manners—and I would still shrink from such talk.","If what you say were true, it would mean that Shu had never changed its dress and Ba had never reformed its customs. Even I cannot bear to hear such an argument.","巴不化俗 means Ba would not have transformed its customs; “Ba Han manners” wrongly fuses Ba with Han and drops the verb 化.","high","applied"],
    ["s0042","idiomatic","now you would yoke them to the tribes of the west. Popular strength is spent; we doubt the task can ever be completed. That would be the envoys' legacy as well, and we tremble for your advisors.","now you would link them with the tribes of the west. The people's strength is exhausted, and we fear the work cannot be completed. This would also become a liability for you as envoy, and we privately fear for you.","使者 is the single envoy being addressed, Sima Xiangru; 累 is a burden or liability, not a legacy, and 左右 is a respectful circumlocution for the addressee here.","medium","applied"],
    ["s0207","literal","In cover Zhou leaped fish, fell grain vessel, rested them with burning.","For Zhou, a fish leaped into the boat, and it was marked as auspicious with a burnt offering.","蓋 is the particle “for/indeed,” and 躍魚隕杭 is the Zhou omen of a fish leaping into the boat (杭=舟), then honored with 燎; the original is nonsense, but the proposal wrongly invents “grain” falling into a vessel.","high","applied"],
    ["s0207","idiomatic","The house of Zhou received its sign when fish leaped into the king's boat and grain filled the vessel—then offered them up with fire.","The house of Zhou received its sign when a white fish leaped into King Wu's boat, and he offered it to Heaven in a burnt sacrifice.","The parallel accounts and Yan Shigu's note identify a white fish leaping into King Wu's boat and being offered to Heaven; the source contains no grain or second offering.","high","applied"]
  ],
